doc:sch-2-sec-10 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "10 Pre-existing interconnection rights" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If, immediately before the commencement of section 137 of the Telecommunications Act 1991, a carrier within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1989 had, under section 49 of the Telecommunications Act 1989 or section 10A of the AUSSAT Act 1984, a right to interconnect its facilities to another carrier’s network on payment of an amount agreed between them or determined by AUSTEL, the payment of that amount is a term and condition for the purposes of the right of the first-mentioned carrier to interconnect its facilities to that other carrier’s network under section 137 of the Telecommunications Act 1991 and is taken to have been agreed or determined as mentioned in paragraph 137(2)(b) of that Act." ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991-sch-2-sec-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "11 Pre-existing class licences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-11 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Until class licences are issued under section 209 of the Telecommunications Act 1991, services supplied after the    Telecommunications (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1991 Compilation date: 1/7/16 Registered: 18/7/16  commencement of that section in accordance with class licences within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1989 that were issued under section 75 of that Act and were in force immediately before the repeal of that section are taken to be supplied under class licences issued under the first-mentioned section.  (2) This section has effect subject to section 12 of this Act." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Until class licences are issued under section 209 of the Telecommunications Act 1991, services supplied after the    Telecommunications (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1991 Compilation date: 1/7/16 Registered: 18/7/16  commencement of that section in accordance with class licences within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act 1989 that were issued under section 75 of that Act and were in force immediately before the repeal of that section are taken to be supplied under class licences issued under the first-mentioned section.  (2) This section has effect subject to section 12 of this Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f9720c6cd6dec35208b5ca08c315a8ed668c0c541279e6febc991e78f02aaf3a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
