concept:telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991-sch-2-sec-1989 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1989 AUSTEL had commenced, but had not concluded and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-1989 ;
    values:originalText "reported on, an investigation under that Part, AUSTEL may complete and report on the investigation in accordance with that Part.  (2) Where before the repeal of Part 6 of the Telecommunications Act 1989 the Minister had requested AUSTEL to conduct an investigation under that Part but AUSTEL had not concluded and reported on the investigation, AUSTEL must commence, or continue, as the case may be, and conclude and report on, the investigation in accordance with that Part.    Telecommunications (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1991  Compilation date: 1/7/16 Registered: 18/7/16  (3) Part 6 of the Telecommunications Act 1989 continues in force for the purposes of this section." ;
    skos:definition "reported on, an investigation under that Part, AUSTEL may complete and report on the investigation in accordance with that Part.  (2) Where before the repeal of Part 6 of the Telecommunications Act 1989 the Minister had requested AUSTEL to conduct an investigation under that Part but AUSTEL had not concluded and reported on the investigation, AUSTEL must commence, or continue, as the case may be, and conclude and report on, the investigation in accordance with that Part.    Telecommunications (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1991  Compilation date: 1/7/16 Registered: 18/7/16  (3) Part 6 of the Telecommunications Act 1989 continues in force for the purposes of this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "41c05b5aebd5c8494d5c974e480ef0a9bcb1bf1c4b41b0de54a73ad24bb3b28d" ;
