concept:telecommunications-transitional-provisions-and-consequential-amendments-act-1991-sch-2-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Existing regulations under Telecommunications Act 1989"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (3), any regulations made under section 185 of the Telecommunications Act 1989 and in force immediately before the repeal of that section continue in force as if made under section 406 of the Telecommunications Act 1991.  (2) A reference in a regulation so continued in force to a provision of the Telecommunications Act 1989 is taken to be a reference to the corresponding provision of the Telecommunications Act 1991.    Telecommunications (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1991 Compilation date: 1/7/16 Registered: 18/7/16  (3) This section does not apply to a regulation the making of which would not be authorised by the Telecommunications Act 1991." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subsection (3), any regulations made under section 185 of the Telecommunications Act 1989 and in force immediately before the repeal of that section continue in force as if made under section 406 of the Telecommunications Act 1991.  (2) A reference in a regulation so continued in force to a provision of the Telecommunications Act 1989 is taken to be a reference to the corresponding provision of the Telecommunications Act 1991.    Telecommunications (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 1991 Compilation date: 1/7/16 Registered: 18/7/16  (3) This section does not apply to a regulation the making of which would not be authorised by the Telecommunications Act 1991."@en ;
